Added `AIModel.kind`, which records whether a model is for chat or for embedding. A chat model and an embedding model are not interchangeable and are not the same endpoint. This app now refuses a retrieval feature that is configured with a chat model, before any network traffic, in place of a confusing provider-side error later. The default is `chat`, so each record that existed before keeps its meaning. The Discover AI Models job leaves the field at its default, because `GET /v1/models` has no field that says which kind a model is.
